n> <span class="w" data-strong="G2596">against</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G5216">you</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G5574">falsely</span>, <span class="w" data-strong="G1752">for</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G1700">my</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G1752">sake</span>.</span>  <span class="verse" data-osis-id="MAT 5:12" data-n="12"></span> <span class="woj"><span class="w" data-strong="G5463">Rejoice</span>, <span class="w" data-strong="G2532">and</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G21">be exceeding glad</span>: <span class="w" data-strong="G3754">for</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G4183">great</span> <span class="added">is</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G5216">your</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G3408">reward</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G1722">in</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G3772">heaven</span>: <span class="w" data-strong="G1063">for</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G3779">so</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G1377">persecuted they</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G4396">the prophets</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G3588">which were</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G4253">before</span> <span class="w" data-strong="G5216">you</span>.</span></p><br class="p">
#### verses ####
5:1-1 marker=/0/7/0 start=/0/7 end=/0/7/30 "And seeing the multitudes, he went up into a mountain: and when he was set, his disciples came unto him:"
5:2-2 marker=/0/7/31 start=/0/7/31 end=/0/7/47 "And he opened his mouth, and taught them, saying,"
5:3-3 marker=/0/7/48 start=/0/7/48 end=/0/7/52 "Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven."
5:4-4 marker=/0/7/53 start=/0/7/53 end=/0/7/57 "Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted."
5:5-5 marker=/0/7/58 start=/0/7/58 end=/0/7/62 "Blessed are the meek: for they shall inherit the earth."
5:6-6 marker=/0/7/63 start=/0/7/63 end=/0/7/67 "Blessed are they which do hunger and thirst after righteousness: for they shall be filled."
5:7-7 marker=/0/7/68 start=/0/7/68 end=/0/7/72 "Blessed are the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy."
5:8-8 marker=/0/7/73 start=/0/7/73 end=/0/7/77 "Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see God."
5:9-9 marker=/0/7/78 start=/0/7/78 end=/0/7/82 "Blessed are the peacemakers: for they shall be called the children of God."
5:10-10 marker=/0/7/83 start=/0/7/83 end=/0/7/87 "Blessed are they which are persecuted for righteousness’ sake: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven."
5:11-11 marker=/0/7/88 start=/0/7/88 end=/0/7/92 "Blessed are ye, when men shall revile you, and persecute you, and shall say all manner of evil against you falsely, for my sake."
5:12-12 marker=/0/7/93 start=/0/7/93 end=/0/9 "Rejoice, and be exceeding glad: for great is your reward in heaven: for so persecuted they the prophets which were before you."
chapter_verses: [0, 0, 0, 0, 12]

